<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Yamanaka et al. (2023), Miao et al. (2023) & Adhyapok et al. (2021) epithelial somite rosette vertex mechanics and mesenchymal-to-epithelial transition (MET) model — MorphoEval overall 91.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `2021-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling.py` (91.9/100, up from 60.1/100 in Pass 1; +31.8 overall). The remediated script implements a 2D 32-vertex apico-basal differential interfacial tension L-BFGS-B relaxation solver for an N=16 wedge-cell somite rosette, reproducing exact agreement with the analytical polygon equilibrium ratio (WT L_ap/L_bas = 0.3030 vs 0.3030 analytical and 0.305 empirical), Y-27632 ROCK-inhibited lumen dilation (L_ap/L_bas = 0.7013, R_in* = 19.65 um vs 7.72 um in WT), and Minus-Matrigel depolarization (0.5562), evaluating all 6 experimental regimes from Yamanaka et al. (2023), Miao et al. (2023), and Adhyapok et al. (2021) (Pearson r = 0.9989, RMSE = 0.0086), quantifying EphA4/ephrinB2 inter-somitic cleft separation (S_cleft = 0.8189 vs 0.0930 in Eph/ephrin KD), mapping the 2D phase diagram over apical tension and Matrigel concentration, and segmenting bilateral somite rosettes on `somitoid_rosette_specimen.jpg` (45.38 px spacing, CV = 0.2010, dome/cleft contrast = 1.189x), backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_029_somitoid_chirality_buckling.lean`. Overall 91.7/100 (faithfulness 91.7, reproducibility 91.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 89, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 93, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/somitoid_chirality_buckling_comparison.png: rendered output of 2021-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 788839 B, 2253×1554 px, artifact_sha256 aae2e04bd0e93a9f8f9601a3be10f47f48c37dd75e58e945e9ad68b46b51fdfc (sha256 aae2e04bd0e93a9f8f9601a3be10f47f48c37dd75e58e945e9ad68b46b51fdfc), spec_fingerprint 834555c3491ff9a0813c6b8298d939c224a2f6c75546f46b11089139cd1ede3c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 834555c3491ff9a0813c6b8298d939c224a2f6c75546f46b11089139cd1ede3c; artifact_sha256: aae2e04bd0e93a9f8f9601a3be10f47f48c37dd75e58e945e9ad68b46b51fdfc; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/somitoid_chirality_buckling/scout_manifest.json=8326704c93aa8a75..., datasets/somitoid_chirality_buckling/somitoid_chirality_buckling_reference.json=89cec9bd5a9ed6ba..., datasets/somitoid_chirality_buckling/somitoid_rosette_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-somitoid-chirality-buckling-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Yamanaka et al. (2023) Nature 614:509-520 & Miao et al. (2023) Nature 614:500-508 discovery that Matrigel ECM embedding and RhoA/ROCK-dependent apical actomyosin constriction drive epithelial somite rosette polarization and central somitecoel lumen formation in human axioloids and somitoids | Adhyapok et al. (2021) Dev. Cell 56:1312-1324 mechanical vertex/cellular-Potts model demonstrating that combined apical constriction (gamma_ap > gamma_bas) and EphA4/ephrinB2 heterotypic boundary repulsion (gamma_het > gamma_hom) govern somite rounding and inter-somitic cleft separation | Y-27632 ROCK inhibition or absence of Matrigel ECM abolishes the apico-basal tension differential (gamma_ap -> gamma_bas) and prevents polarized epithelial somite rosette morphogenesis; reconstructed_in_script: 2D 32-vertex apico-basal differential interfacial tension relaxation solver for an N=16 wedge-cell somite rosette matching the exact analytical polygon equilibrium ratio (WT L_ap/L_bas = 0.3030 vs 0.3030 analytical and 0.305 empirical) | 6-regime experimental perturbation series (WT +10% Matrigel, Calpeptin hyper-constriction, Low 2.5% Matrigel, EphA4/ephrinB2 knockdown, Y-27632 ROCK inhibition, and Minus-Matrigel control; Pearson r = 0.9989, RMSE = 0.0086) | EphA4/ephrinB2 inter-somitic cleft sorting energy barrier (Delta_E_cleft = 75.60 pN, S_cleft = 0.8189 in WT vs 0.0930 in Eph/ephrin KD), 2D phase diagram over (gamma_ap/gamma_lat, Matrigel %), and bilateral somite rosette segmentation on somitoid_rosette_specimen.jpg (45.38 px mean spacing, CV = 0.2010); transfer_boundary: 2D cross-sectional vertex mechanics of an N-cell epithelial somite rosette and Young-Dupre inter-somitic cleft balance compared with dorsal vertebrate somite SEM metameric periodicity; does_not_claim: Full 3D sclerotome/dermomyotome lineage regionalization following late somite maturation." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple MESP2/RIPPLY2 wavefront arrest directly from a live HES7 delayed oscillator into the spatiotemporal activation of EphA4/ephrinB2 and RhoA/ROCK line tensions.",
        "remediation needed: Extend the 2D cross-sectional wedge-rosette vertex model to a 3D apical-basal polyhedral scutoid shell to capture 3D somitecoel lumen pressurization." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.17e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

